      "summaries": {
        "en": "Stable Diffusion is an open-source latent text-to-image diffusion model that generates high-quality images from text descriptions, making AI-powered creative tools accessible to developers and artists. It operates by gradually denoising random noise in a compressed latent space, which is computationally efficient compared to pixel-space diffusion. You can experiment with it locally using provided notebooks, fine-tune it on custom datasets for specific styles, or integrate it into applications for content creation, design prototyping, and educational demos.",
        "zh": "Stable Diffusion 是一个开源的潜在文本到图像扩散模型，能够根据文字描述生成高质量图像，为开发者和创作者提供了可访问的AI创意工具。其核心创新在于在压缩的潜在空间中逐步去噪生成图像，相比像素空间扩散大幅降低了计算需求，使得在消费级硬件上运行成为可能。你可以通过提供的Jupyter Notebook在本地快速体验，针对特定风格微调自定义数据集，或将其集成到内容创作、设计原型和教育演示等实际应用中，探索文本与视觉的创造性连接。",
        "es": "Stable Diffusion is an open-source latent text-to-image diffusion model that generates high-quality images from text descriptions, making AI-powered creative tools accessible to developers and artists. It operates by gradually denoising random noise in a compressed latent space, which is computationally efficient compared to pixel-space diffusion. You can experiment with it locally using provided notebooks, fine-tune it on custom datasets for specific styles, or integrate it into applications for content creation, design prototyping, and educational demos.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "stable-diffusion gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Stable Diffusion is an open-source latent text-to-image diffusion model that generates high-quality images from text descriptions, making AI-powered creative tools accessible to developers and artists. It operates by gradually denoising random noise in a compressed latent space, which is computationally efficient compared to pixel-space diffusion. You can experiment with it locally using provided notebooks, fine-tune it on custom datasets for specific styles, or integrate it into applications for content creation, design prototyping, and educational demos.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/CompVis/stable-diffusion for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
